\newlabel{fig:ConformalSealing}{{7}{308}{The conformal sealing of the Jang bubbles. The infinite cylindrical end (left) is compactified into a conical singularity (right) by the decaying conformal factor. The cone angle satisfies $\Theta > 2\pi $ (angle excess); however, the singularity has zero $p$-capacity for $1 < p < 3$ and is therefore removable for the AMO analysis}{figure.7}{}}
