\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The conformal sealing process. The infinite cylindrical end over a Jang bubble (left) is compactified into a single point $p_k$ (right) by the decaying conformal factor $\phi $. Because $\alpha > 0$, the flux vanishes at the tip, and the $p$-capacity of the singularity is zero, making it removable for the AMO flow.}}{308}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conical}{{8}{308}{The conformal sealing process. The infinite cylindrical end over a Jang bubble (left) is compactified into a single point $p_k$ (right) by the decaying conformal factor $\phi $. Because $\alpha > 0$, the flux vanishes at the tip, and the $p$-capacity of the singularity is zero, making it removable for the AMO flow}{figure.8}{}}
